    [Feature][Worker] Allow probabilistic draft sampling with MRV2 PCP (#18086)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Ascend MRV2 PCP rejects `draft_sample_method="probabilistic"` during
    configuration validation, preventing it from reaching the existing draft
    sampling implementation. Remove the greedy-only check for MTP, Eagle3
    and DSpark.
    
    Update the PCP configuration tests to accept both `greedy` and
    `probabilistic` for these methods and remove the cases expecting the
    greedy-only error. The speculative-method allowlist and other PCP
    configuration checks remain in place.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Ascend MRV2 PCP configuration validation now accepts probabilistic
    draft sampling for MTP, Eagle3 and DSpark. Independent restrictions,
    including fine-grained LM-head TP constraints, still apply.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Updated `tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py` to cover both
    sampling methods for MTP, Eagle3 and DSpark across the existing eager
    and graph configuration cases. The current CPU unit-test runs are
    pending for both the verified vLLM main commit and v0.30.0.
    - Passed `ruff check vllm_ascend/worker/v2/pcp_manager.py
    tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py`.
    - Passed `ruff format --check vllm_ascend/worker/v2/pcp_manager.py
    tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py`.
    - Passed Python AST syntax checks for both changed files and `git diff
    --check`.
    - The GitHub Actions `pre-commit` job passed for commit `42af4588c`,
    including PR title validation, the full repository pre-commit hooks and
    `mypy`. NPU inference has not been run on this commit.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
